+/**
+ * Marks the given layer as having received content encoded with a codec other
+ * than H.264 during the frame currently being accumulated. Image operations
+ * will not be suppressed for that frame, even where they overlap regions
+ * carried by the H.264 stream.
+ *
+ * Suppression assumes the H.264 stream is the sole source of truth for the
+ * regions it covers, which is false whenever another codec paints over the
+ * same area. Callers should invoke this for every surface command that is not
+ * H.264.
+ *
+ * @param layer
+ *     The layer that received non-H.264 content.
+ */
+void guac_display_layer_mark_mixed_codec(guac_display_layer* layer);
